{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "43788666",
      "title": "Module Summary",
      "lectureOrder": 64,
      "videoOrder": 60,
      "sourceHash": "400376b169a3e570536fbbafeb89bd8e013d31e118e2ad8f9521cf141ed1d00f",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0,
          "end": 4.14,
          "en": "So in this section, you now learned a lot about Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.14,
          "end": 8.07,
          "en": "You actually learned all about the crucial essentials",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.07,
          "end": 10.86,
          "en": "every Angular developer must know.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.86,
          "end": 13.68,
          "en": "You learned about Components, why they matter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.68,
          "end": 16.26,
          "en": "and that the idea is that you build",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.26,
          "end": 19.83,
          "en": "potentially complex user interfaces with Components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.83,
          "end": 22.08,
          "en": "And you learned how to create Components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.08,
          "end": 24.78,
          "en": "That there are classes that are decorated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.78,
          "end": 26.67,
          "en": "with that Component decorator,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.67,
          "end": 28.83,
          "en": "which then holds the configuration",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.83,
          "end": 32.4,
          "en": "for a Component, like its identifier, you could say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.4,
          "end": 35.58,
          "en": "its selector, but also where to find the template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.58,
          "end": 37.26,
          "en": "or styles of a Component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.26,
          "end": 39.18,
          "en": "Because a Component, in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 39.18,
          "end": 43.05,
          "en": "is a custom HTML element, you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.05,
          "end": 46.5,
          "en": "And the idea then is that you can use that element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.5,
          "end": 49.17,
          "en": "in the templates of other Components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 49.17,
          "end": 52.56,
          "en": "so that you're building a Component tree in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 52.56,
          "end": 55.5,
          "en": "Now these Components can then also talk to each other",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 55.5,
          "end": 58.17,
          "en": "with help of Inputs and Outputs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 58.17,
          "end": 61.44,
          "en": "Inputs are, in the end, properties of a Component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 61.44,
          "end": 64.47,
          "en": "that can be set from outside that Component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 64.47,
          "end": 66.66,
          "en": "So from inside the parent Component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 66.66,
          "end": 69.45,
          "en": "which uses the other Component in its template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 69.45,
          "end": 70.8,
          "en": "And Outputs are, in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 70.8,
          "end": 72.777,
          "en": "custom events that can be emitted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 72.777,
          "end": 74.7,
          "en": "and that can also contain data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 74.7,
          "end": 77.78999999999999,
          "en": "so that a child Component can talk back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 77.78999999999999,
          "end": 79.17,
          "en": "to its parent Component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 79.17,
          "end": 82.28999999999999,
          "en": "and let it know about something that happened inside of it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 82.28999999999999,
          "end": 84.33,
          "en": "which is a crucial feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 84.33,
          "end": 88.32,
          "en": "Now since things are happening in an Angular app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 88.32,
          "end": 90.84,
          "en": "users might be clicking buttons and so on,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 90.84,
          "end": 93.24000000000001,
          "en": "it's also quite common that data changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 93.24000000000001,
          "end": 94.47,
          "en": "in your Angular app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 94.47,
          "end": 96.57,
          "en": "and therefore you might wanna output",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 96.57,
          "end": 99.69,
          "en": "that dynamic data in the templates of your Components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 99.69,
          "end": 103.5,
          "en": "which you can do with various template binding syntaxes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 103.5,
          "end": 106.65,
          "en": "like with string interpolation, which can be used to,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 106.65,
          "end": 109.44,
          "en": "for example, output the value stored in a property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 109.44,
          "end": 110.91,
          "en": "of your class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 110.91,
          "end": 114.84,
          "en": "Or if you want to set a property of some DOM element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 114.84,
          "end": 116.34,
          "en": "like the source of an image,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 116.34,
          "end": 118.71000000000001,
          "en": "you can do that with property binding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 118.71000000000001,
          "end": 120.51,
          "en": "If you wanna listen to events,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 120.51,
          "end": 123.51,
          "en": "no matter if they're custom events or built-in events,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 123.51,
          "end": 125.31,
          "en": "you do that with event binding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 125.31,
          "end": 128.13,
          "en": "where you use these parentheses around the event name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 128.13,
          "end": 129.6,
          "en": "and you then define the code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 129.6,
          "end": 132.45,
          "en": "that should be executed when the event occurs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 132.45,
          "end": 135.87,
          "en": "By the way, a special kind of binding is two-way binding,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 135.87,
          "end": 139.17000000000002,
          "en": "which is typically used in conjunction with form inputs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 139.17000000000002,
          "end": 140.22,
          "en": "which is unlocked",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 140.22,
          "end": 143.37,
          "en": "by using this special two-way binding syntax",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 143.37,
          "end": 145.5,
          "en": "on properties that support it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 145.5,
          "end": 146.79,
          "en": "Most properties don't,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 146.79,
          "end": 150.54,
          "en": "but one property that does is the ngModel property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 150.54,
          "end": 153.36,
          "en": "which is offered by the ngModel directive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 153.36,
          "end": 155.55,
          "en": "which is available once you import it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 155.55,
          "end": 157.62,
          "en": "and unlock the FormsModule.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 157.62,
          "end": 159.87,
          "en": "You can then use the ngModel directive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 159.87,
          "end": 162.15,
          "en": "with its two-way binding syntax",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 162.15,
          "end": 165.75,
          "en": "to set up this two-way communication on an Input element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 165.75,
          "end": 168.69,
          "en": "for example, which allows you to listen to changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 168.69,
          "end": 172.38,
          "en": "whilst also being able to send back data into the Input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 172.38,
          "end": 174.48,
          "en": "to update it, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 174.48,
          "end": 177.32999999999998,
          "en": "Now coming back to data that changes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 177.32999999999998,
          "end": 179.91,
          "en": "it's worth noting that by default,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 179.91,
          "end": 182.7,
          "en": "Angular watches for possible events",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 182.7,
          "end": 184.74,
          "en": "that could lead to data changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 184.74,
          "end": 187.59,
          "en": "and therefore UI changes automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 187.59,
          "end": 191.19,
          "en": "with help of an internal package called zone.js.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 191.19,
          "end": 192.57,
          "en": "And therefore, by default,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 192.57,
          "end": 195.63,
          "en": "all you have to do if you wanna update the UI",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 195.63,
          "end": 197.37,
          "en": "is change some data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 197.37,
          "end": 199.65,
          "en": "for example, after a button click,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 199.65,
          "end": 202.38,
          "en": "and output that data in the template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 202.38,
          "end": 205.65,
          "en": "with help of one of the template binding features,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 205.65,
          "end": 207.96,
          "en": "and Angular will figure out the rest,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 207.96,
          "end": 209.67000000000002,
          "en": "which is pretty convenient.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 209.67000000000002,
          "end": 213.3,
          "en": "You can, however, also use Signals instead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 213.3,
          "end": 216.42000000000002,
          "en": "where Angular is not automatically watching",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 216.42000000000002,
          "end": 219.78,
          "en": "for all kinds of events that could lead to changes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 219.78,
          "end": 223.95,
          "en": "but where you instead explicitly notify Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 223.95,
          "end": 226.02,
          "en": "about changes by, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 226.02,
          "end": 229.41,
          "en": "calling the set method on a Signal value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 229.41,
          "end": 232.95,
          "en": "And where Angular sets up a subscription",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 232.95,
          "end": 235.02,
          "en": "whenever you read a Signal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 235.02,
          "end": 237.9,
          "en": "so that it knows which places of your app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 237.9,
          "end": 240.6,
          "en": "are interested in those data changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 240.6,
          "end": 242.94,
          "en": "and should potentially be updated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 242.94,
          "end": 246.3,
          "en": "And this, whilst being a bit more work for you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 246.3,
          "end": 249.27,
          "en": "the developer, can therefore be a more efficient",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 249.27,
          "end": 251.31,
          "en": "State management mechanism",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 251.31,
          "end": 254.55,
          "en": "and can potentially lead to better performance.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 254.55,
          "end": 256.41,
          "en": "Though this Signals approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 256.41,
          "end": 259.8,
          "en": "is only available since Angular version 16,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 259.8,
          "end": 262.14,
          "en": "and therefore in older Angular projects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 262.14,
          "end": 264.21,
          "en": "you, for example, can't use it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 264.21,
          "end": 267.15,
          "en": "Now it's also quite common that, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 267.15,
          "end": 268.53,
          "en": "when some data changes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 268.53,
          "end": 271.35,
          "en": "you wanna render some content conditionally",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 271.35,
          "end": 273.18,
          "en": "only if a certain condition is met.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 273.18,
          "end": 275.1,
          "en": "And you can do that in Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 275.1,
          "end": 278.01,
          "en": "by using the @if template syntax,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 278.01,
          "end": 280.47,
          "en": "which also, however, is only available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 280.47,
          "end": 282.63,
          "en": "since Angular version 17.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 282.63,
          "end": 286.23,
          "en": "Before that, you had to use the special ngIf directive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 286.23,
          "end": 288.9,
          "en": "which was a bit more clunky to use however,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 288.9,
          "end": 291.24,
          "en": "especially if you don't just have a if case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 291.24,
          "end": 292.86,
          "en": "but also potentially some else",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 292.86,
          "end": 295.71,
          "en": "or else if cases you want to handle.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 295.71,
          "end": 298.89,
          "en": "Also common is that you wanna output some list data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 298.89,
          "end": 301.17,
          "en": "and you wanna repeat some part of the DOM",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 301.17,
          "end": 304.17,
          "en": "for every element in an array, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 304.17,
          "end": 307.59,
          "en": "This can be done with the @for template syntax,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 307.59,
          "end": 310.2,
          "en": "which makes it easy to loop through all the items",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 310.2,
          "end": 312.66,
          "en": "in an array and output some markup",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 312.66,
          "end": 314.76,
          "en": "for every element in that array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 314.76,
          "end": 317.22,
          "en": "This feature is also only available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 317.22,
          "end": 319.08,
          "en": "since Angular version 17,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 319.08,
          "end": 321.57,
          "en": "and therefore in older Angular versions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 321.57,
          "end": 324.66,
          "en": "you would use the ngFor directive instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 324.66,
          "end": 327.93,
          "en": "Other features we had a look at in this section were,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 327.93,
          "end": 331.05,
          "en": "for example, how to dynamically add or not add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 331.05,
          "end": 332.82,
          "en": "a CSS class to an element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 332.82,
          "end": 335.85,
          "en": "with help of that special class binding syntax.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 335.85,
          "end": 339.36,
          "en": "We also had a look at the special ng-content element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 339.36,
          "end": 341.7,
          "en": "which is offered by Angular, which in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 341.7,
          "end": 345.48,
          "en": "allows you to define a slot in the markup of a template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 345.48,
          "end": 347.67,
          "en": "that will be used to render the content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 347.67,
          "end": 350.13,
          "en": "that's passed between the tags of that Component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 350.13,
          "end": 351.81,
          "en": "which can be really useful.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 351.81,
          "end": 354.57,
          "en": "And we also, for example, had a look at pipes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 354.57,
          "end": 358.11,
          "en": "which make it easy to format and transform values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 358.11,
          "end": 359.73,
          "en": "you are outputting in the template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 137,
          "start": 359.73,
          "end": 361.68,
          "en": "like for example, the date pipe,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 138,
          "start": 361.68,
          "end": 364.05,
          "en": "which can help with date formatting,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 139,
          "start": 364.05,
          "end": 366.87,
          "en": "another feature that's built into Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 140,
          "start": 366.87,
          "end": 370.05,
          "en": "Another problem you commonly have to deal with",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 141,
          "start": 370.05,
          "end": 373.08,
          "en": "is the submission of forms and how to handle that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 142,
          "start": 373.08,
          "end": 376.41,
          "en": "And that's, again, a place where Angular helps you",
